------- FILE main.asm
------- FILE sync.asm LEVEL 2 PASS 3
      0  38f8					      include	"sync.asm"
      1  38f8							; Fat Chip 64 - device sync (v0.13): the keytar (Yamaha SHS-10) and Synthcart
      2  38f8							;
      3  38f8							; Menu, DEVICE SYNC (defaults first):
      4  38f8							;   TEMPO FROM      KEYTAR / OWN / SYNTHCART
      5  38f8							;		     KEYTAR: its MIDI clock (24 a beat, sent even while stopped)
      6  38f8							;		     sets the tempo, averaged over beats (the clock jitters about
      7  38f8							;		     4 ms). Without a clock for 300 ms, Fat Chip's own tempo
      8  38f8							;		     (B taps) is back. SYNTHCART: taps and beat tempos snap to
      9  38f8							;		     Synthcart's ten NTSC tempos (whole Atari frames a beat).
     10  38f8							;   START/STOP      KEYTAR / OWN: its Start and Stop start / stop the beat demo
     11  38f8							;		     (a start waits for the next beat clock: step 1 lands on it)
     12  38f8							;   RHYTHM BUTTONS  PICK BEAT / IGNORE: its style (Program Change on channel 16)
     13  38f8							;		     picks a beat demo (styleBeat)
     14  38f8							;   DRUM NOTES      IGNORE / PLAY: its drum notes on the MidiNES (drums.asm)
     15  38f8							;   VOICE BUTTONS   PICK SOUND / IGNORE: its voice (Program Change 0-24 on the
     16  38f8							;		     key channel) picks a sound (voiceSound)
     17  38f8							;   WHEEL	     BEND / OFF: +-BEND RANGE on everything (bend.asm)
     18  38f8							;   VIBRATO / PORTAMENTO / SUSTAIN BUTTON  an action each (CC 1 / 65 / 64,
